    <string name="privacy_policy">Privacy policy</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_text">Lumo Browser does not collect analytics or telemetry and has no account system.\n\nStays on your device: history, bookmarks, tabs, downloads list, site settings, preferences, the optional diagnostic log, and the encrypted AI key. They are excluded from cloud backup.\n\nLeaves your device only when you act: pages you visit (to those sites), searches (to your chosen search engine), Safe Browsing checks (Google, via Android WebView, can be turned off), filter-list updates (to the list URL you configure), translation (page address to your configured provider), and AI requests (page text to your configured endpoint, after confirmation).\n\nPrivate tabs use a separate WebView profile: their history is never written, and their cookies, storage and cache are deleted when the last private tab closes. Files you download in a private tab stay in your downloads folder.\n\nFreedom uses your device\'s ordinary internet connection. It contains no VPN, proxy or tunnelling and cannot bypass network-administrator or site restrictions.</string>
    <string name="private_explainer">Private tabs don\'t save history, and their cookies and site data are deleted when you close the last private tab. Downloads and bookmarks you create are kept. Your network administrator, internet provider and the sites you visit can still see your activity.</string>
